+/**
+ * The player as the media session should see it.
+ *
+ * A server transcoding on the fly answers without a length, and ExoPlayer
+ * files a progressive stream whose length and duration are both unknown under
+ * "live" (`ProgressiveMediaPeriod.setSeekMap`). media3 then refuses to say
+ * where such a stream is: the playback state it publishes carries position -1
+ * and speed 0, so the system's controls, the lock screen and anything reading
+ * the session sit at 0:00 for the whole song while the app's own progress
+ * moves (#135). The second play of the same track was fine, which is the
+ * confusing part of the report: by then Navidrome serves the transcode it
+ * cached, with a length.
+ *
+ * A track whose length we were told is not live, whatever the stream looks
+ * like, and saying so is all it takes to get the position back. That is
+ * exactly the case this covers: `durationMs` is set from the queue for every
+ * song and left out for a radio, which is the thing that really is live and
+ * keeps the player's own answer.
+ *
+ * Nor can the player seek such a source, and it says so: the commands it
+ * offers carry no seek, so the system's controls, the car and the watch drew
+ * a bar nobody could drag while the app's own slider worked. The app is what
+ * makes those seeks work — it asks the server for the stream starting where
+ * you pointed — so the session offers the seek on its behalf
+ * (`onSeek`) whenever the track has a length to seek within. A radio, which
+ * has none, keeps the player's answer and stays undraggable, as it should.
+ *
+ * `positionOffsetMs` is the other half of that: a stream re-requested at
+ * 2:00 is a new source, and the player counts it from zero. The app knows
+ * where it really is and says so here, so the session and the app agree on
+ * one clock instead of drifting apart at every seek. Position, buffer and
+ * duration all move with it, since they are read against each other. It
+ * stays at zero for everything else.
+ */
+private class MediaSessionPlayer(
+  player: Player,
+  private val positionOffsetMs: () -> Long,
+  private val onSeek: ((Long) -> Unit)?,
+) : ForwardingPlayer(player) {
+  /** Does whoever queued this track know how long it is? (a radio does not) */
+  private fun hasKnownDuration(): Boolean = currentMediaItem?.mediaMetadata?.durationMs != null
+
+  override fun isCurrentMediaItemLive(): Boolean =
+    if (hasKnownDuration()) false else super.isCurrentMediaItemLive()
+
+  /** Can the source itself be seeked, or does it have to be asked for again? */
+  private fun playerCanSeek(): Boolean =
+    super.getAvailableCommands().contains(Player.COMMAND_SEEK_IN_CURRENT_MEDIA_ITEM)
+
+  override fun getAvailableCommands(): Player.Commands {
+    val commands = super.getAvailableCommands()
+    if (onSeek == null || !hasKnownDuration()) {
